# Chapter 3: Shared Database

The project is currently at **Chapter 3**. The system still uses a **shared database**.

Database separation per service is covered in **Chapter 4**. Do not introduce it prematurely.

## When generating code

- Keep the shared database as-is in examples and refactors.
- Do not split databases, add per-service datasource configs, or introduce database-per-service patterns unless explicitly requested.
- Patterns (strangler fig, bounded contexts, service extraction, etc.) should assume one shared database for now.

## When to separate databases

Only refactor to separate databases when the user **explicitly requests** Chapter 4 work or database separation.
